# AI Governance Practice — environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. Never commit real values;
# `.gitignore` covers `.env.local` and everything else matching `.env*`.
#
# All variables are OPTIONAL. With none of them set the app runs in local mode:
# every feature works and progress is saved in the browser. Adding Supabase
# credentials turns on accounts and cross-device sync.
#
# NOTE: every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is inlined into the client bundle at BUILD
# time, not read at runtime. Changing one in Vercel requires a redeploy to take
# effect, and none of them may hold a secret.

# --- Supabase (optional: enables auth + progress sync) ----------------------
# Project Settings → API keys in the Supabase dashboard.
#
# The key is the publishable / anon key — the one intended to reach browsers.
# Both formats work: the current `sb_publishable_...` format and the legacy
# `eyJ...` anon JWT. Never put the service role or secret key here; it would be
# inlined into the client bundle and readable by anyone.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here

# --- Auth redirect ----------------------------------------------------------
# Where Supabase email-confirmation links return the user. No trailing slash;
# the app appends `/login`.
#
# Required in production. Without it, confirmation links fall back to the
# Supabase project's default Site URL, and the mobile build has no window
# origin to fall back to at all.
#
# Must also be registered in Supabase -> Authentication -> URL Configuration ->
# Redirect URLs, or Supabase rejects the redirect.
#   local:  http://localhost:3000
#   Vercel: https://your-domain.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.vercel.app

# --- Emailing results (optional) -------------------------------------------
# Turns on "Send results to email" on the completed-results screen. Leave it
# unset and the button explains that delivery is not configured; the PDF
# download works either way and needs no server.
#
# There is deliberately no provider API key here. Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is
# inlined into the browser bundle, so a mail provider's key placed here would
# be readable by anyone who loads the page. This variable holds a URL only; the
# credentials live at the other end of it.
#
# The endpoint must accept POST with a JSON body:
#
#   {
#     "to":      "learner@example.com",
#     "subject": "Your AIGP practice exam results",
#     "text":    "<plain-text summary; no answer key>",
#     "summary": { "mode", "sittingId", "completedAt", "total", "correct",
#                  "incorrect", "unanswered", "percentage", "elapsedMs" }
#   }
#
# and return 2xx once the message is accepted for delivery. It must allow CORS
# from NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL (and from the Capacitor origin for the app build).
#
# The reference implementation is a Supabase Edge Function, since Supabase is
# already an optional dependency here and a second vendor is not warranted for
# one feature: create a function that reads `to`, `subject` and `text`, hands
# them to whichever mail provider you have, and keeps that provider's key in
# the function's own secrets. Then point this variable at its URL. Rate-limit
# it — it takes an arbitrary address and sends mail.
#
# Nothing about the address is stored by the app: it is typed on the results
# screen, used for one request, and cleared. Do not log it at the endpoint.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RESULTS_EMAIL_ENDPOINT=

# --- Seeding only (server-side; never expose to the client) -----------------
# Used by `npm run seed` to write the question bank into the database.
# Deliberately has no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, so it is never inlined into the
# browser bundle. Do not add this to Vercel unless you run the seed there.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
